# CLI Orchestration

`cli.py` is a dispatcher only. Add flags on the parser, then forward argv into the matching `src/` script. Do not put prediction or training logic in `FootballAnalyticsCLI`.

## Task → required modules

| Task | `src/` modules |
|---|---|
| `full-league` | `automate_football_analytics_fullLeague.py`, `algorithms.py`, `ml_training.py`, `ml_evaluation.py` |
| `single-match` | `automate_football_analytics.py`, `algorithms.py` |
| `download` | `download_all_tabs.py` |
| `download-fixtures` | `fixtures_downloader.py` |
| `organize` | `organize_structure.py` |
| `validate` | `check_downloaded_data.py` |
| `corners` | `corners_analysis.py`, `automate_corner_predictions.py` |
| `analyze-corners` | `corners_analysis.py` |
| `view` | `view_suggestions.py` |
| `backtest` | `analyze_suggestions_results.py` |
| `convert-upcoming` | `convert_upcoming_matches.py` |

When adding a task: update `REQUIRED_MODULES`, add a `task_*` method, and register the choice on `--task`.

## Flag pitfalls

- `--leagues` is a comma list. `--league ALL` without `--use-parsed-all` looks for `football-data/all-euro-football/ALL.csv` and fails.
- `--use-parsed-all` reads `todays_fixtures_<YYYYMMDD>` from `data/analysis/` then `data/`.
- Team names for `--home` / `--away` / `--home-team` are case-sensitive and must match historical CSVs.

See `ReadMeDocs/QUICK_REFERENCE.md` and skill `complete-analysis-pipeline`.
